// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO5 (Vext power-gate), GPIO8-11 (LoRa SPI
// bus), GPIO12-14 (LoRa RST/BUSY/DIO0), GPIO38-40/47/48 (TFT display) -
// see vendor pins_arduino.h.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO21 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard USER_KEY
// button (vendor schematic HT-VMT190 vmt190V0.5.SchDoc: S3 "USER_KEY"
// wired to GPIO21 with pull-up R22). GPIO0 is also a physical button
// (S2 "BOOT_KEY") but is the reserved boot-strapping pin, left untagged.
// No onboard user-controllable LED confirmed - LED1 is an automatic
// battery-charge indicator wired to the charger IC (not GPIO-driven);
// LED2 is wired directly onto the GPIO0/BOOT_KEY net (not an
// independently drivable output) - neither tagged.
